urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ffd0efbbddc8e23e699c8a870eeb0016eb81cb3c.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued September 22 at 7:40PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 740 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 9\nmiles south of Bennett, or 29 miles east of Denver, moving north at\n20 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and pea size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nAurora, northeastern Centennial, Bennett, Manila Village, Watkins,\nStrasburg, Arapahoe Park and Byers.","ends":"2026-09-22T20:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet; Central and East Adams and Arapahoe Counties","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.25cc7f3ada9031ef41c607717b43d4ea5782a1eb.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.25cc7f3ada9031ef41c607717b43d4ea5782a1eb.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued September 22 at 7:33PM MDT until September 22 at 10:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"FFWBOU\n\nThe National Weather Service in Denver has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nWestern Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nNortheastern Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 1030 PM MDT.\n\n* At 733 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Between\n0.5 and 2 inches of rain have fallen. Flash flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, gulches,\nroads, and poor drainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nEastern Centennial, eastern Highlands Ranch, northern Castle Rock,\nParker, Greenwood Village, Lone Tree, Castle Pines, The Pinery,\nFoxfield and Cherry Creek Reservoir.","ends":"2026-09-22T22:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Western Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8317f4f140c23cd2dcc15b37cf36ddb416458f82.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8317f4f140c23cd2dcc15b37cf36ddb416458f82.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued September 22 at 6:40PM MDT until September 22 at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...South Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...\nSouth Central Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nCentral Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry creeks. Water over some\nroadways.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 639 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Minor flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area.\nBetween 0.5 and 1.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nCastle Rock, Parker, Lone Tree, Roxborough Park, Sedalia,\nLouviers, Castle Pines, Sprucewood, Devil's Head, The Pinery,\nDeckers, Cheesman Reservoir and Shamballa.","ends":"2026-09-22T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b063d162dd6264109e8d955c7c55d6a3682dd990.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b063d162dd6264109e8d955c7c55d6a3682dd990.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-23T00:39:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 230039 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discu